            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0243" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5 Submarines/24: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-08T20:00:00-05:00">October 8, 1936—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>367. Your 462, October 6, 2 p.m. You are authorized to sign the procès-verbal
                    designed to obtain further accessions to the rules of international law
                    concerning submarine warfare. Full Power has been signed by the President and is
                    being mailed by pouch today.</p>
                <p>Should it be desired to sign the procès-verbal before the receipt of the Full
                    Power, it is hoped that the present telegram will be considered sufficient
                    evidence of your authority to sign that instrument.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
